I have found that progress in Nethack is exponential -- when you first
start out, you get killed over and over and over again, but as you keep
playing you eventually pick up speed and get killed less and less until
you can start ascending, then ascending repeatedly.  After that I
suppose you move to slash 'em or start trying conducts that are more
and more insane (I don't THINK anyone  has yet ascended a blind,
illiterate, atheist wishless polyless genoless vegan pacifist but I
suppose someone has tried).

So don't be discouraged.  This is normal.

The two hints I would give are both out of game:

1. SLOW DOWN.  Not just in-game but out of game as well.  Take your
time between moves and think about what you want to do and how.
That's the lesson I learned from Krysia's Krusader -- when you're
surrounded by soldier ants and down to 5 HP don't simply die. Instead,
step away from the computer for a smoke or cookie break.   Calm down.
Think about your options.  Look at your inventory.    I can't tell you
the number of times I've been killed because I didn't think, when my
boots of Jumping or my scroll of teleportation or wand of digging would
have saved me.

The reason nethack is turn-based instead of realtime is to give people
time to think when they're in these positions. The single greatest
advantage you have over the computer is your head and the luxury of as
much time to ponder your situation as you wish.


2. Every time you get killed, don't start another game until you
understand just what killed you and why.  When you're sure you know
what you did wrong, then you can go back into the dungeon prepared to
avoid that mistake in future.  No point in making the same mistake over
and over, is there?  

Good luck!



